#. All current battle type slots are tested, including an added third type; target and species-default types do not choose the branch.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:summary"
msgid "The effect depends on the user’s current type."
msgstr ""

#. Condition on the move user. Full approved type:ghost name is Привидение; native label Дух is a shortened form.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:ghost"
msgid "Ghost type present"
msgstr ""

#. Condition on the move user; includes every non-Ghost current type combination.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:other"
msgid "Ghost type absent"
msgstr ""

#. User cost uses current maximum HP; target residual uses base maximum HP. Separate Dynamax note states this distinction. {hp} uses existing localized HP key: RU ОЖ.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:ghost_effect"
msgid "The user loses half its maximum {hp} and curses the target. At the end of each turn, the cursed target loses a quarter of its maximum {hp}."
msgstr ""

#. All changes affect the user. Existing localized Attack/Defense/Speed keys fill the holes, RU Атака/Защита/Скорость. Normal shared ability modifiers and stage caps apply; not percentage or raw-stat changes.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:other_effect"
msgid "Normally raises the user’s {attack} and {defense} by one stage and lowers its {speed} by one stage."
msgstr ""

#. Both HP calculations floor their fractions and apply MathMax(1,...). Cost is charged without checking current HP against it; attacker faint command follows.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:rounding"
msgid "{hp} loss is rounded down, with a minimum of 1 {hp}. The user can faint from the cost."
msgstr ""

#. Ghost branch only. It fails before adding curse or charging user HP; no claim about all possible semi-invulnerable interactions.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:failure"
msgid "Fails if the target is already cursed."
msgstr ""

#. Ghost residual only. Approved ability:magic-guard is Магзащита; no claim about type, damage-dealing moves or the separate HP cost.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:magic_guard"
msgid "Magic Guard prevents the end-of-turn damage."
msgstr ""

#. Ghost residual calls GetBaseMaxHP, which removes the current Dynamax HP multiplier. {hp} is localized HP. Does not describe Z-Curse bonuses or Max Move conversion.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:curse:dynamax"
msgid "End-of-turn damage ignores the {hp} increase from Dynamax."
msgstr ""

#. Summary of the environment table on the Secret Power card; the added-effect chance stays in the Effect line.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:secret_power:summary"
msgid "The added effect depends on the battle environment."
msgstr "L’effet secondaire dépend de l’environnement du combat."

#. Summary of the environment table on the Nature Power card; the table lists the called move.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:nature_power:summary"
msgid "Uses another move that depends on the battle environment."
msgstr "Utilise une autre capacité qui dépend de l’environnement du combat."

#. Both current types become the table type and an added third type is cleared; the move fails when any current type already matches.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:camouflage:summary"
msgid "Makes the type of the battle environment the user’s only type. Fails if the user already has that type."
msgstr "Fait du type de l’environnement du combat le seul type du lanceur. Échoue si le lanceur a déjà ce type."

#. Condition checked first, before every other rule. RU names follow the game's terrain move names Поле тока, Поле травы, Поле тумана, Поле разума.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:terrain"
msgid "Electric, Grassy, Misty or Psychic Terrain is active"
msgstr "Un Champ Électrifié, Herbu, Brumeux ou Psychique est actif"

#. Refers to the first four rows of the table below.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:terrain_effect"
msgid "The row of that terrain applies."
msgstr "La ligne de ce champ s’applique."

#. Battle types the engine treats as indoors for these three moves; Battle Frontier covers its tower, sands and circus battles.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:building"
msgid "Battle Frontier, link, Trainer Tower or e-Reader battle"
msgstr "Combat de la Zone de Combat, en link, de la Tour Dresseurs ou e-Reader"

#. The quoted row name must match the translation of the Building environment.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:building_effect"
msgid "The Building row applies."
msgstr "La ligne « Bâtiment » s’applique."

#. Fallback condition after the terrain and building rules.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:other"
msgid "Any other battle"
msgstr "Tout autre combat"

#. The notes below explain how the environment is chosen, in order of precedence.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:other_effect"
msgid "The row of the battle environment applies."
msgstr "La ligne de l’environnement du combat s’applique."

#. A script variable chosen before the battle; the area and surfing changes still apply to its value.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:note_script"
msgid "An event script can set the environment of a battle; it takes precedence over the rules below."
msgstr "Un script d’événement peut fixer l’environnement d’un combat ; il prime sur les règles suivantes."

#. Shown below the environment table; map changes do not clear the script variable.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:note_script_persistence"
msgid "The value of the script variable persists across maps until a script rewrites it."
msgstr "La valeur de la variable de script est conservée d’une carte à l’autre jusqu’à ce qu’un script la réécrive."

#. Checked by the map, only for trainer battles; the quoted row name must match the Champion's room environment.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:note_champion"
msgid "Trainer battles in the Champion’s room use the Champion’s room row."
msgstr "Les combats de Dresseurs dans la salle du Maître utilisent la ligne « Salle du Maître »."

#. The battle scene is a map header setting: gym, special room and the Elite Four rooms.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:note_scene"
msgid "Otherwise a map with its own battle scene uses the row of that scene."
msgstr "Sinon, une carte avec sa propre scène de combat utilise la ligne de cette scène."

#. Tile behaviour first (grass, sand, mountain, water), then cave, underwater, sea-route and indoor map types override it.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:note_tile"
msgid "Otherwise the tile under the player and the map type at the start of the battle choose the environment."
msgstr "Sinon, la case sous le joueur et le type de carte au début du combat choisissent l’environnement."

#. Autumn, winter, desert and swamp areas, Antisis and Dehara, and the surfing variants of the rows. RU сёрф follows move:surf.
msgctxt "page:mechanics:environment:rule:note_area"
msgid "Seasonal and named areas and surfing then change the environment as the table states."
msgstr "Ensuite, les zones saisonnières ou particulières et le Surf changent l’environnement comme l’indique le tableau."

